{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact head 96d0862b55766879bd0c7a2ffe5411feff15e3a3. Rebuilt, not carried.\n\nYou were right to refuse the carry. The old head's artifact and review request described a main that no longer existed, and re-basing would have moved the commit without re-checking the claims — which is exactly the difference that matters here, because the two real defects in this round were claims, not anchors.\n\nBoth verified in the code rather than accepted from your list. The fold emits open, promised, reported, satisfied, stale, cancelled, reneged and withdrawn; requested and dangling are not among them, so the page invented two states a reader could look for and never find. And WorkDrawer renders the word local for a trailer-only association, so unverified trailer named a marker nobody would ever see. I kept the distinction the prose was drawing, because it is correct — a trailer is ordinary commit text and the log will not vouch for it — and fixed only the word and the claim about the view.\n\nThe browser-only worktree section moves to gs serve, which documents the view and now holds the UI and service anchors that make its claims checkable. See also is last on every page touched. main's ack.md, say.md and baseline are untouched.\n\nThe known-failing list falls to 23 and I checked the direction three ways rather than the total: nine entries removed, five lost pages, none gained a page, none added. The gate refused to pass until the nine were deleted.\n\nGates: make docs passes, the full suite passes, go vet silent, go build clean, git diff --check clean, one commit on current main and zero behind.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a39ea4401ad1d45bbde7ec13e349cff6d194da3c","branch":"request/docs-behavior-rebuild","head":"96d0862b55766879bd0c7a2ffe5411feff15e3a3","status":"ready-for-review"}}